course: dictionary
lesson: 309
title: The word anatomy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anatomy is a noun for the parts of a body and how they are arranged. In science, human anatomy covers the bones, the heart, the lungs and other organs. Doctors and artists both study anatomy.
explain: The word can also mean a close, careful study of something, like «the anatomy of a crime». Books use it in titles such as «The Anatomy of …» to show a detailed study.
explain: Look at the context: «What looks like a horse's backward knee is really its ankle; its knee is higher up, and artists study anatomy so legs look right.» The sentence compares the parts of a horse's leg, so anatomy means the body structure of an animal.
fact: Anatomy means the study of the parts of the body and how they are arranged.
fact: Anatomy can also mean the body structure of a person, animal or plant, as in «the anatomy of a frog».
fact: Anatomy can mean a close, careful study of something, as in «the anatomy of a crime».
fact: Anatomical means to do with anatomy, and an anatomist is a person who studies anatomy.
fact: Informally and humorously, anatomy can mean a part of the body, as in «He hurt a delicate part of his anatomy».
exercise: What does anatomy mean in science? | The making of medicine | The study of stars and planets | *The study of the parts of the body and how they are arranged | A way of cooking meat
exercise: In «What looks like a horse's backward knee is really its ankle», what is being compared? | Cooking and eating | The weather | *Parts of a horse's body | Two different kinds of horse
exercise: Which word means a person who studies anatomy? | *anatomist | anatomy | anatomical | anatomies
test: In «The Anatomy of …», what kind of study does the title suggest? | A song with a catchy tune | A cooking recipe | *A detailed study | A fast race
test: Which word is an adjective meaning to do with anatomy? | *anatomical | anatomist | anatomies | anatomy
exam: In «He hurt a delicate part of his anatomy», what does anatomy mean? | A close study of a crime | A type of bone in the arm | A plant that grows in water | *A part of the body, said in a humorous way
